notes.content:
Hey all, long time no see!

A new [b]Revamped Controls Menu[/b] is the first of many important updates that are coming to the game in the near future.

- Controls are now grouped by function into neat sub-menus;
- Some of the controls have been renamed for clarity;
- You can now define a key to take an in-game screenshot (the screenshots will be saved in ../steamapps/common/Vangers/data folder in your Steam directory);
- Auto-Acceleration toggle is now available in the Controls Menu as well as in "Pause" menu;
- ...and other various small fixes and optimizations.

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/5944467/35f7617ee53b321358dd4954e9a76bd6b5823e4b.jpg[/img]

Also, a [b]new default control scheme[/b] has been developed by the veteran members of our community.
It is meant to organize the default controls into a more coherent layout that works on most keyboards and has some resemblance to existing modern RPG game layouts. Hopefully, this will be helpful to newer players, who tend to find the controls in the game a bit unwieldy.

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/5944467/0f5b1a018a9a35041d08ad3cf03f34836985f760.png[/img]

[b]IMPORTANT NOTICE:[/b] [u]This update will overwrite your old controls file[/u]. You’ll have to redefine them in-game, we're sorry for any inconvenience this causes. This had to be done to allow our new players to start the game without fighting with the weird old default controls.

[url=https://discord.gg/GTCvhdq]Join our Discord[/url] if you want to keep in touch with the Vangers community. We have added an international channel where vangers will be able to get any game-related help or just hang out with other fellow wheelers.
